{{redirect|Greater rage|the monster ability|Rage (monster ability)}}

{{feat
|type=class
|prereq=[[barbarian]]
|desc=The barbarian may '''rage''', gaining a +4 morale bonus to [[strength]] and [[constitution]] and +2 to all [[will]] [[saving throw]]s, in exchange for a -2 penalty to [[armor class]]. The barbarian may use this ability once per day at first [[class level|level]], +1 use per day at level 4, and every 4 levels thereafter, extending into [[epic class|epic]] levels.<br />
At 15th level, the rage ability becomes '''greater rage''', giving the barbarian +6 to strength and constitution and +3 to will saves (the -2 penalty to armor class still applies).
|use=selected
|icon=ife_rage.gif
|class1=barbarian
}}

==Notes==

*The duration is the barbarian's constitution [[modifier]] (before the rage) plus 7 [[round]]s, plus an extra 2 rounds for ''greater rage''.
*Ability bonuses are [[ability cap|capped]] at +12, so a PC already gaining ability bonuses from items, spells or potions, might gain less than the full bonuses from ''rage''/''greater rage''.
* The armor class penalty is a [[dodge bonus]], so (due to a bug) it is lost when [[flat-foot]]ed.
*Barbarian rage is similar to, but not the same as, the [[rage (monster ability)|rage ability]] of some creatures, such as [[badger]]s. (For example, creatures do not suffer an armor class penalty.)
* The temporary constitution increase means that a character who is low on [[hit point]]s at the end of the rage can drop into the negatives when the bonus expires.

'''See also:''' [[mighty rage]], [[terrifying rage]], [[thundering rage]]

